From dcbfbacaed50b2a884dbe8e595939752ce170f18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:41:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/49] audit: physical access-audit map, with a CPU access

The map was coco3-only at first: -audit on any other machine allocated
the map, recorded nothing, and wrote a well-formed all-zero file --
worse than refusing, because the output looks like a run that touched no
memory.  Every input the composition needs (mem_class, irq_depth) lives
in the shared 6809 core, so the bit composition moves to audit.h as
audit_bits_mc6809() and the Dragon family marks too, beside its
physical-watchpoint checks, with the logical address standing in for the
physical -- the same degrade those watchpoints already use on a flat
machine.  Machines whose cpu_cycle is overridden (Deluxe CoCo, Dragon
Professional, iMMUnity) are not marked, matching exactly where physical
watchpoints already do not fire.  The MC-10 stays out because the 6803
core has no access classification at all -- inherent, not silent.
